}}

==Overview==
After finishing the trials of the [[Great Plateau]] during the "[[EX The Champions' Ballad]]" [[Main Quest]], the [[One-Hit Obliterator]] will split into four glowing orbs and scatter to different areas of [[Hyrule Kingdom|Hyrule]], revealing four ancient structures called [[Monument]]s. One of the Monuments appears at [[East Gerudo Mesa]], southeast of the [[Divine Beast Vah Naboris]]. As [[Link]] approaches the Monument, he will hear the voice of a [[Monk]], who explains that each pillar displays a [[Map]] that reveals the location of a trial that must be undertaken in the [[Gerudo (Region)|Gerudo]] [[Region]].<ref>{{Cite|{{Color BotW|Monk Blue|I applaud your courage in coming here. The locations that will be revealed to you are of trials that will enhance the power sleeping within. Do not let your guard down...}}|Monk|BotW}}</ref>

[[Kass]], who is nearby, will make a remark about either the flash of light or the Monument, depending on how many Monuments Link has already visited.<ref>{{Cite|What was that...flash of light? Perhaps it was my imagination playing tricks on me.|Kass|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|Did that {{Color BotW|Blue|stone monument}} just start glowing? I suppose that proves I didn't imagine it the first time.|Kass|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|This {{Color BotW|Blue|stone monument}} has survived for 10,000 years. What secrets does it hold...|Kass|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|That light... Is it a reaction to someone nearby? Is it me...or is it...|Kass|BotW}}</ref> When he Link, he is at first confused why someone else would venture to such a high altitude.<ref>{{Cite|Hm? How strange to see someone else at this ample altitude. I wonder what brought him here...|Kass|BotW}}</ref> Kass apologizes to Link for voicing his thoughts aloud, as he has become used to speaking to himself.<ref>{{Cite|Oh! How embarrassing. I'm afraid traveling on my own encourages me to talk to myself on occasion.|Kass|BotW}}</ref> Kass notes that the Monument is the same one mentioned in the [[Unfinished Song]] of his teacher.<ref>{{Cite|Look! As expected, there's one here too! One of the {{Color BotW|Blue|monuments}} mentioned in my teacher's {{Color BotW|Blue|unfinished song}}.|Kass|BotW}}</ref>{{Note|If this is the first Monument that Link has visited, Kass will explain that it was mentioned in an Unfinished Song written by his teacher.<ref>{{Cite|This {{Color BotW|Blue|monument}}... I must admit it has taken me by surprise! My teacher's {{Color BotW|Blue|unfinished song}} mentions such {{Color BotW|Blue|monuments}}, and now one has appeared before my eyes...|Kass|BotW}}</ref> At Link's confusion, Kass explains that it is missing its key verses.<ref>{{Cite|[Unfinished song?] Yes. The song is mostly complete. However... My teacher left this world without finishing the {{Color BotW|Blue|key verses}}.|Kass|BotW}}</ref> He is now on a journey to finish the song.<ref>{{Cite|I wish the weave the missing pieces together and finish the song.|Kass|BotW}}</ref>}} He is happy to be able to sing so close to Divine Beast Vah Naboris.<ref>{{Cite|Ah, such a rush of happiness I feel at being able to sing while the {{Color BotW|Blue|Divine Beast}} watches over us...|Kass|BotW}}</ref>

Part of the Unfinished Song references the trials that [[Urbosa]] overcame.<ref>{{Cite|The song my teacher left behind... There's {{Color BotW|Blue|a verse}} about the trials that {{Color BotW|Blue|Champion Urbosa}} overcame.|Kass|BotW}}</ref> He then proceeds to sing him the song, which provides instructions for completing all three trials.<ref>{{Cite|♪Lightning king of the desert.<br/>{{Color BotW|Blue|Naboris}}'s Champion, the stalwart.♪<br/>♪The hero's power shall grow.<br/>Seek trials {{Color BotW|Blue|monuments}} show.♪<br/>♪One, {{Color BotW|Red|fight the brute of the sand}}.<br/>Two, {{Color BotW|Red|chase rings upon the land}}.♪<br/>♪Three, {{Color BotW|Red|throw the orb underground}}.<br/>Champion, trials abound!♪|Kass|BotW}}</ref> After, Kass asks if Link was moved by his performace.<ref>{{Cite|...So? Did it move you?|Kass|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|...So? Did the {{Color BotW|Blue|verse}} move you? It was written in honor of the {{Color BotW|Blue|Champion}} challenging the trial.|Kass|BotW}}</ref> His research into legends about the Champions has allowed him a deeper understanding of who they were,<ref>{{Cite|By steeping myself in legends of the {{Color BotW|Blue|Champions}}, I'm beginning to form a deeper understanding of them.|Kass|BotW}}</ref> which will in turn help him with completing the key verses.<ref>{{Cite|This will prove invaluable in writing the {{Color BotW|Blue|key verses}} of the song.|Kass|BotW}}</ref> Kass feels as though the Champions are speaking to him through the song and asking for its completion.<ref>{{Cite|Hmm... It's as though the Champions are speaking to me through the song... I hear their silent plea for its completion. That's why I must learn more about the Champions of Hyrule's past...|Kass|BotW}}</ref> He has been able to hear tales about Urbosa from [[Riju]] and [[Buliara]],<ref>{{Cite|Luckily, the {{Color BotW|Blue|Gerudo}} chief, {{Color BotW|Blue|Riju}}, and her guard, {{Color BotW|Blue|Buliara}}, shared some precious tales of their Champion with me.|Kass|BotW}}</ref> though he had to leave his [[Gerudo Outfit|comfort zone]] in order to meet them.<ref>{{Cite|I'm grateful I was able to visit {{Color BotW|Blue|Gerudo Town}}, even though I had to... well, leave my comfort zone a bit.|Kass|BotW}}</ref> Once he is done speaking, the [[Main Quest]] will begin.

Link can complete the trials in any order. By defeating the [[Molduking]] in the [[East Barrens]], he will unlock [[Keive Tala Shrine]]. [[Sand Seal]] surfing through a series of [[Glowing Ring]]s in the [[West Barrens]] will reveal [[Takama Shiri Shrine]]. Finally, retrieving a [[Sacred Orb]] from the [[Yiga Clan Hideout]] and throwing it into the [[Yiga Clan Hideout Chasm]] outside will unearth [[Kihiro Moh Shrine]].

Each of the [[Ancient Shrine]]s reward Link with one of [[Naboris's Emblem]]s.<ref>{{Cite|{{Color BotW|Monk Blue|Your resourcefulness in overcoming this trial speaks to the promise of a hero. In the name of the Goddess Hylia, I bestow upon you this gift... Naboris's Emblem.}}|Monk|BotW}}</ref> The Monk of the Shrine will then inform Link that collecting all three Emblems will unlock a new challenge.<ref>{{Cite|{{Color BotW|Monk Blue|Collect three emblems to open the path to a new challenge.}}|Monk|BotW}}</ref> They will tell Link how many more trials he has to complete before fading away.<ref>{{Cite|{{Color BotW|Monk Blue|Two remain...}}|Monk|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|{{Color BotW|Monk Blue|One remains...}}|Monk|BotW}}</ref> After completing all three shrines, the [[Monk]] of the final Shrine will instruct him to go to Divine Beast Vah Naboris.<ref>{{Cite|{{Color BotW|Monk Blue|Now that you have collected three emblems, you must go to Divine Beast Vah Naboris...}}|Monk|BotW}}</ref>

When Link arrives at [[Spectacle Rock]], he will once again hear the voice of a Monk. The voice informs him that in exchange for Naboris's Emblems, he will be taken to the [[Illusory Realm]], a world within his memories, to face a trial.<ref>{{Cite|{{Color BotW|Monk Blue|To the one who approaches this Divine Beast... In the name of the Goddess Hylia, I offer this trial. In exchange for Naboris's Emblems... you will be granted the chance to tread through the realm of memories.}}|Monk|BotW}}</ref> Without determination, Link will find this trial to be unforgiving.<ref>{{Cite|{{Color BotW|Monk Blue|Those who lack determination will find this trial unforgiving.}}|Monk|BotW}}</ref> The Monk also reminds him to take this world seriously, as its truth is deeper than it appears.<ref>{{Cite|{{Color BotW|Monk Blue|Do not take this place lightly, nor dismiss it as merely a world within your mind. The truth is much deeper than you know.}}|Monk|BotW}}</ref>

Link will then find himself inside Naboris, where the Monk reiterate that this realm was made from his memories.<ref>{{Cite|{{Color BotW|Monk Blue|This illusory realm was created from the depths of your memories...}}|Monk|BotW}}</ref> The [[Enemy]] that he will fight is a product of his own fear, which he must overcome during this trial.<ref>{{Cite|{{Color BotW|Monk Blue|The enemy you shall face is a product of the fear that dwells within. This battle is a trial of the soul. You must emerge victorious using only the tools provided.}}|Monk|BotW}}</ref> With this, [[Thunderblight Ganon]] appears again.

