After defeating the phantasm again, Link will return to the exterior of Divine Beast Vah Naboris, where he will find Kass.<ref>{{Cite|Well, well. Though our aims are different, our feet took us to the same destination. I speak figuratively, of course. I travel by wing rather than by foot.|Kass|BotW}}</ref> He explains that hearing anecdotes about Urbosa has inspired him to write a song for her, which brought him to the [[Divine Beast]].<ref>{{Cite|Ah! Wandering around here and listening to anecdotes about {{Color BotW|Blue|Champion Urbosa}} has truly invigorated me. In fact, it has inspired me to honor her in my own way, separate from my teacher's {{Color BotW|Blue|unfinished song}}. That is why I felt inclined to roost here, near the {{Color BotW|Blue|Divine Beast Vah Naboris}}, which {{Color BotW|Blue|Urbosa}} herself mastered.|Kass|BotW}}</ref> He then sings "[[Champion Urbosa's Song (Song)|Champion Urbosa's Song]]".<ref name="Urbosa's Song">{{Cite|♪Recall {{Color BotW|Blue|Naboris}}'s Champion of sand,<br/>before she was lost to the land.♪<br/>♪Chief {{Color BotW|Blue|Urbosa}}'s heart was strong,<br/>so the princess came along.♪|Kass|BotW}}</ref> This allows Link to visualize the "[[Champion Urbosa's Song (Memory)|Champion Urbosa's Song]]" [[Recovered Memory]] from 100 years ago.<ref name="Urbosa's Song"/> 

After the Memory ends, Kass notes that, while Urbosa was a fierce warrior, she was also a good friend to [[Princess Zelda|Zelda]].<ref>{{Cite|Hmm... Though she was a fierce warrior, the Gerudo chief was also a loving friend of Hyrule's princess.|Kass|BotW}}</ref> He asks Link what he thought of the song,<ref>{{Cite|So? What do you think of {{Color BotW|Blue|Champion Urbosa's Song}}?|Kass|BotW}}</ref> which he explains allowed him to feel closer to his teacher.<ref>{{Cite|By writing a song that honors the heart of Champion Urbosa, I feel closer than ever to my dear teacher.|Kass|BotW}}</ref> Link will then hear the voice of Urbosa, who calls him an impressive voe and allows him wield [[Urbosa's Fury]] more often.<ref>{{Cite|I must say, you are an impressive voe. You may now wield Urbosa's Fury far more often.|Urbosa|BotW}}</ref> The skill will be upgraded to [[Urbosa's Fury +]], which reduces its recharge time to four minutes. She leaves the duty of protecting Zelda to Link.<ref>{{Cite|You are the pride of Hyrule, hero. Take care of our princess. I'm leaving that honor in your capable hands.|Urbosa|BotW}}</ref> After receiving the upgrade, the Main Quest is completed.

